    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0300" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6354/220: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-15">May 15,
                        1940</date>.<lb/>[Received May 15—2:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1220. The Colonial Office states that it has seen American newspaper reports to
                    the effect that Mr. Hopkins<anchor n="53" xml:id="d357-f1"/> is looking into the
                    tin situation with a view to increasing American stocks; it pointed out that the
                    next meeting of the Tin Committee would be on May 27 and that if American
                    Government purchases are to be made it would be one of the relevant factors to
                    be taken into consideration at that meeting. The Colonial Office indicated it
                    would accordingly appreciate being advised prior to the meeting if there is any
                    intention to make such purchases.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d357-f1" n="53" xml:id="d357-f1-content">
                <p>Harry Hopkins, Secretary of Commerce until September 1940.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
